cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PHOENIX and TERN: a protocol-driven framework for task-based human-AI software-development studies"
abstract: >-
  PHOENIX connects study design, participant capture, and analysis handoff
  through a single versioned YAML protocol. Researchers design and review a
  study in a web workspace; TERN runs the configured session in VS Code; the
  server joins editor events, surveys, and optional external measurements into
  one dataset for export to a notebook. Because capture configuration and the
  analysis plan are derived from the same protocol, a planned measure cannot go
  unrecorded and an analysis cannot be planned over data the study never
  collects.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/idreesshaikh/human-ai-studies-framework"
